Game Description OH DEMON! Fix my TV is about how a banal everyday task turns into a surreal adventure beyond the bounds of reason. The main tool for interacting with the world is the protagonist’s gaze, with the help of which the environment is transformed: from discovering hidden clues and turning on lights to activating secret passages. The project is a unique combination of comedic elements and scary moments, where the atmosphere of horror is achieved largely through the sound design. A specially created audio language heightens the tension, and the musical accompaniment dynamically adapts to the action, enhancing both moments of pure fear and epic clashes with opponents.
The plot is extremely simple: an elderly woman calls upon a demonic entity to fix her TV. The protagonist in this unusual narrative is precisely this summoned creature. However, in OH DEMON! Fix my TV this seemingly trivial request becomes the starting point for a journey through impossible spaces. The gamer will have to explore locations that defy logic and overcome sophisticated obstacles. On the way you will encounter otherworldly creatures, confronting which will require ingenuity and quick reaction. Solving numerous puzzles becomes the key to moving through this absurd and dangerous world.
Game Screenshots &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;

Game Description Super Woden: Rally Edge is an arcade racing simulator, the central element of which is the passage of a large-scale single-player campaign. The basis of all gameplay is the career mode, built on the principles of classic racing projects. The path to the top begins with the purchase of a used car, and the money earned in racing becomes a source for its subsequent modernization or the purchase of faster models. The competition takes place on tracks in six different countries, challenging drivers to demonstrate their skills on asphalt, gravel or snow surfaces. The racing program is not limited to standard rally stages, including gymkhana-style tests and high-speed hill climbs.
The fleet includes hundreds of stylized low-poly cars, which, being fictional, with their outlines refer to famous and rare examples of the automotive industry. In addition to the single player experience, Super Woden: Rally Edge offers competitive split-screen multiplayer for up to 4 people. For those who like to set records, there are time trials with online leaderboards, and weekly challenges add additional variety to the process. There is also a photo mode for creating spectacular photos. The visual design of the project is made in the retro style of the 90s, which is complemented by support for modern high-resolution monitors and frame refresh rates.
Game Screenshots &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;

Game Description SHE WAS 98 is a depressing psychological horror with a first-person view, forcing you to face the horrors of a fading consciousness within the walls of a dilapidated apartment. The space, once filled with coziness, is now an oppressive labyrinth of old things, faded photographs and painful memories. The main character arrives in this place with a noble goal - to provide care for his almost hundred-year-old grandmother. Abandoned by other relatives, the elderly woman is completely dependent on her grandson for help. Doctors make a diagnosis that explains the strange behavior of her with progressive dementia. However, it soon becomes clear that what is happening within these walls goes far beyond the usual illness, hiding something more sinister.
The narration is told from the first person, which provides maximum immersion into the growing nightmare. Instead of fighting monsters, SHE WAS 98 offers exploration of cramped spaces, where every creaking floorboard and dark corner becomes a source of paranoia. The oppressive atmosphere is created not through sudden frightening moments, but through the slow build-up of suspense and a feeling of constant psychological pressure. The main task is to carry out everyday errands, but routine actions turn into a collision with something irrational. The line between reality and hallucinations is gradually blurring, forcing one to doubt the adequacy of not only the elderly woman, but also the protagonist himself.
Game Screenshots &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;

Game Description NIGHTBELL is a first-person psychological horror that immerses you in the unsettling atmosphere of Christmas night, when the usual feeling of safety in your own home is replaced by a feeling of constant threat. Exploration of a once cozy home becomes a central mechanic, as familiar rooms and corridors are transformed beyond recognition, and shadows and sounds take on an ominous character. The gameplay forces you to constantly seek shelter from unknown danger, carefully listening to your surroundings. To move forward, you will have to follow the mysterious ringing of the bell and piece together scattered clues to understand the true nature of the events taking place.
The story is told from the perspective of a little boy who stayed with his mother on a festive evening, waiting for a miracle. The starting point of the nightmare is a story about a witch heard before going to bed. Waking up in the middle of the night from an ominous ringing, the protagonist discovers the sudden disappearance of his mother. Soon after, he comes face to face with a creature that eerily resembles her appearance. The NIGHTBELL project leaves behind an alarming aftertaste, because when morning comes, everything that happened seems like just a child’s dream. However, some details of what happened do not fit into the framework of a harmless nightmare, casting doubt on the reality of the experience.
Game Screenshots &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;

Game Description Log.in is about diving into the mind of a criminal who has to face the consequences of his own actions. The narrative suggests taking on the role of an antagonist directly involved in the case of illegally detaining a person in complete isolation from the outside world. The central mystery becomes the identity of the woman being held captive. We have to find answers to questions about the reasons for her imprisonment, as well as understand the motives that prompt the protagonist to try to eliminate her. All events begin to develop rapidly from the moment you first enter the operating system, and the ending of the story promises to radically change the fate of both the protagonist and his captive.
The entire process of immersing yourself in the history of Log.in is based solely on interaction with the personal computer interface. Assembling a complete picture of what is happening is carried out through a scrupulous study of scattered files hidden in the depths of sterile and cold system folders. Among the sources of information are not only images, videos and email correspondence, but also various applications with text notes. In Login, the main emphasis is on gradually building up suspense. The feeling of anxiety is enhanced not by abrupt moments, but by a quiet and methodical analysis of the content. Hidden inside these catalogs are disturbing records and documents that serve as direct evidence of the crime committed.
Game Screenshots &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;

Game Description Prisoners Of The Ephemeral Kingdom is the story of an ancient Chinese ritual known as the Feather Burning Ritual, during which the line between the worlds of the living and the dead begins to rapidly blur. Fourteen strangers from different parts of the world receive a mysterious invitation to the secluded Mayfly Estate. As night falls, the atmosphere of mistrust and anxiety grows, as the dead return and the living lose their bearings. Guests will have to find out who the organizer of this event is, what the true purpose of the ceremony is and what terrible secret has been kept for more than two thousand years. A blood-soaked spectacle spanning entire eras unfolds unnoticed before them.
Finding themselves captives of this fleeting world, gamers must uncover its many secrets and overcome all challenges. The process of exploring the environment and solving puzzles become the main tools for advancement. The narrative in Prisoners Of The Ephemeral Kingdom unfolds gradually, plunging into the intricacies of the plot and the fate of its inhabitants. The project is a visual novel where interaction with the story is carried out through simple mouse clicks, which contributes to complete immersion in what is happening. This allows you to focus on navigating complex plot twists and turns and understanding the motives of the characters.
Game Screenshots &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;

Game Description ODDCORE is a first-person shooter with roguelike elements, where each session is limited to a strict five-minute limit. Time becomes a key resource and main enemy, since its flow is not interrupted even when interacting with improvement stores. Under the guidance of a friendly mascot named Taimi, made in the form of a clock, the protagonist must clear the numerous rooms of the theme park from deadly damage. The main currency for progress is souls, which can be exchanged for an additional 30 seconds, standard stat upgrades, or instant health restoration by shooting yourself at your feet.
Confronting the threat takes place in procedurally generated rooms with a variety of objectives. In addition to the total destruction of opponents, you have to capture control points, flee from the monster in narrow corridors, or collect walking sunflowers. ODDCORE&rsquo;s arsenal includes not only a starting pistol, but also shotguns and assault rifles, and each weapon has two firing modes. Special gadgets allow you to diversify your tactics: from a parkour tackle and an energy pulse to throw back enemies to an explosive plush toy that serves as bait. During breaks between races, you can visit a small room with arcade machines.
Game Screenshots &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;

Game Description Xenosensory is an incremental project with horror elements, where the main task is to facilitate the evacuation of prisoners from a space prison. The process of neutralizing numerous threats is implemented intuitively: to destroy hostile xenoforms, just hover your cursor over them. Each successful action earns research points, which serve as the main currency for progression. After completing short and sometimes intense rounds, the accumulated meta points can be spent to unlock upgrades. An extensive development tree offers access to a variety of perks, additional activities and useful gadgets. Each such acquisition adds new strategic elements to the gameplay, allowing you to adapt your playstyle to suit yourself.
Events take place in the distant future on board an orbital prison station that has become the target of an attack by unknown life forms. Now monstrous creatures roam the corridors of the complex, mercilessly killing or kidnapping survivors. In addition to the direct threat, there are reports of strange and unexplained anomalies. Passing Xenosensory involves sequential progress through many sectors, each of which has a unique layout and presents special types of opponents. Gradually, the player finds pieces of information that reveal the nightmarish secrets of this place and shed light on the true nature of the disaster that occurred.
Game Screenshots &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;

Game Description Gore In Crayon is a 2D pixelated survival horror game where the main goal is to avoid mortal danger in an intense game of cat and mouse. The project immerses you in an atmosphere of constant persecution, where the visual style, reminiscent of children&rsquo;s drawings with colored pencils, creates an ominous contrast with the events taking place on the screen. The narrative unfolds entirely through visual imagery and action, without a single word or dialogue. Every corner of the stylized environment can become either a life-saving shelter or a deadly trap, which forces you to carefully analyze the situation and quickly make decisions to save your life.
At the center of this silent and depressing story is a child&rsquo;s attempt to survive a night in a house where the only adult poses the main threat. That is why completing Gore In Crayon requires the gamer to have maximum concentration and the ability to predict the next move of his opponent. The outcome of the confrontation directly depends on the attentiveness and actions of the gamer himself, because the ending of the story is not predetermined and can end in one of several options. Any mistake or delay results in brutal and graphic scenes of failure. This entire concentrated experience of horror is packed into about 30 minutes of real time, making you appreciate every moment.
Game Screenshots &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;

Game Description Noosphere is a psychological detective story whose central mechanic is to penetrate the minds of other people to unravel a complex mystery. A key aspect of the entire process is the constant movement between physical reality and the mental worlds of the characters encountered. Despite their superficial similarities, these dimensions have unique structures and contain completely different clues. The process of solving puzzles is entirely built on the careful comparison of numerous inconsistencies between two planes of existence. The main character is a boy who wakes up within the walls of a mysterious laboratory without any memories of his past. It is his innate ability for mental intrusion that becomes a tool for exploring other people&rsquo;s thoughts in search of answers.
Progress along the storyline directly depends on decisions made in dialogues and when examining the environment. Each interaction with non-player characters in Noosphere opens up access to new information and shapes their future attitude towards the protagonist. Any choice made provokes certain reactions and directs the narrative along one of the many available scenario branches. This nonlinear structure determines which of several possible story endings the gamer will ultimately see. The fate of the child and the revelation of all the secrets of the mysterious research institute are in the hands of the user. Repeated playthroughs allow you to discover previously inaccessible details and get closer to understanding the full picture of the events that took place.
Game Screenshots &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;

Game Description Food Processing Simulator is an economic strategy, the central task of which is the construction and subsequent administration of your own food processing plant. Achieving success will require finding the optimal balance between equipment productivity, logical layout of premises and scrupulous inventory control. The basis of the gameplay is the establishment of conveyor lines and the gradual automation of all work processes, from the processing of initial ingredients to the final stage of packaging of finished products. The gamer will need strategic thinking to optimize all stages of the production cycle.
The whole journey begins with a modest workshop, which is destined to transform into a large-scale industrial complex. To ensure smooth functioning in Food Processing Simulator, it is necessary not only to modernize machines and master advanced technologies, but also to competently coordinate the actions of hired employees. Constant physical expansion of production facilities is becoming an urgent need to handle increasingly larger orders and increase capacity. Thus, every management task, from the purchase of raw materials to the shipment of batches, becomes part of a single mechanism for building a prosperous food empire.
Game Screenshots &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;

Game Description Japan Stigmatized Property 2 is a surveillance simulator in which the main goal is to meticulously search for anomalies in Japanese properties with a bad reputation. The protagonist needs to hold out until 5 am, tracking any deviations from the norm through camera lenses. The success of the mission depends on attentiveness: missing a significant number of paranormal events or an excessive number of false alarms inevitably leads to failure. Four new areas are available for inspection, including the abandoned Celine Hotel and the wooden K Residence in Tottori Prefecture, where a man is rumored to have died alone. Each task offers two difficulty modes, allowing you to adjust the intensity of what is happening.
The whole concept revolves around the hard work of a CCTV operator who is forced to face inexplicable forces alone. Japan Stigmatized Property 2&rsquo;s gameplay requires you to constantly switch between standard shooting and night vision mode to closely examine the darkest areas of rooms. Deviations recorded are random and range from spontaneous movement of furniture and materialization of objects to the appearance of hostile spirits. Many of the frightening events take inspiration from Japanese urban folklore, adding an extra layer of authenticity to the proceedings. In addition, some of the phenomena are generated using neural network algorithms, ensuring the unpredictability of each new shift.
Game Screenshots &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;

Game Description BAROQUE Become a Meta Being Revive is an arcade action game set in a gloomy post-apocalyptic universe, where the central role is played by a creature named Gru. This protagonist previously appeared as one of the regular opponents in the original story. The main task is to climb the structure of the Neurotower, which requires refined acrobatic maneuvers and rapid movements in space. The controls are intentionally made intuitive to make the experience accessible to a wide range of enthusiasts. As you move up the locations, you will meet characters familiar from the source material, including Moon and Kato. The success of the passage directly depends on the distance traveled, which determines the value of the reward received.
Earned resources allow you to unlock different variations of the main character, such as Muscular Gru or Medusa-like Gru, with the ability to instantly change his appearance. In addition to the classic mode, where any mistake leads to the end of the attempt, BAROQUE offers a completely new competition format. In Countdown mode, you need to cover the maximum distance in 60 seconds, and the number of revivals within this time is not limited. The visual component is complemented by an alternative camera perspective, which allows you to change the standard top view to a more personal perspective from behind the character. An improved interface and instant restart feature make the process more comfortable and smoother.
Game Screenshots &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;

Game Description The Ogre King, which explores the tragic story of a one-eyed ogre, offers dynamic combat in a 3D world with roguelike elements. Each chapter of the adventure consists of several combat stages, culminating in a confrontation with a powerful boss. The process of strengthening your character is based on collecting weapons and armor, creating useful potions and gradually unlocking new abilities. Even defeat does not lead to a complete loss of what has been achieved, since the accumulated experience and learned skills are preserved. In addition to battles, some stages offer solving simple puzzles to find a way out of the location. Each playthrough becomes a step towards understanding all the mechanics.
The central figure of the story is a protagonist named Thunder, wandering through the fragments of a once great state. Fragments of his past and the hidden truth about the reasons for the decline of the kingdom are presented through special plot inserts, stylized as the pages of an illustrated book. This approach to storytelling in The Ogre King allows you to dive deeper into the emotional component of the adventure. During your journey, you may encounter unexpected challenges that shed light on new aspects of the world and its mysteries. Thus, each attempt not only tests skills, but also brings us closer to revealing the full picture of the events that occurred.
Game Screenshots &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;

Game Description Tomba! 2: The Evil Swine Return Special Edition is a special edition that offers a fresh look at the often overlooked sequel to the legendary platformer. The process of passing has been significantly simplified due to modern innovations. The save anywhere function is now available, eliminating the need to look for special places to record progress. There is also an option to rewind time, allowing you to undo an unsuccessful action or a missed jump. Despite these conveniences, the gameplay has retained its signature complexity and demanding reactions. The mechanics are based on a side-scrolling perspective with direct control of the protagonist. The entire adventure takes place in a fantasy world with a vibrant anime style.
The story begins with the treacherous invasion of the Evil Pigs, who seized neighboring territories. At the same time, Tabby, the protagonist&rsquo;s loyal friend, disappears without any trace. Without wasting a second, the character sets off on a risky journey across the sea to find his comrade and put an end to the invasion. In Tomba! 2, the main task is to save the world from insidious invaders. For fans of the franchise, a special addition has been prepared in the form of a virtual museum. This gallery features a rich selection of archival materials, scanned manuals, promotional posters and high-quality illustrations. You can also find original design documents there.
Game Screenshots &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;

Game Description Vampiress: Eternal Duet is a side-scrolling action game, the gameplay of which is based on constant switching between two forms of the main character. In her vampire form, the protagonist becomes a deadly weapon, armed with a huge scythe. However, staying in this form is associated with a constant loss of health, which forces you to look for balance in battle. Replenishment of vitality occurs only after returning to human form, where the heroine is much more vulnerable and uses the staff to weaken opponents, rather than destroy them. This mechanic forces you to constantly evaluate risks and alternate an aggressive attack with a tactical retreat to regenerate. As you progress, new combat skills are unlocked, allowing you to withstand increasingly serious threats.
Events take place in a gloomy world with neon style, which has become a battleground between people and demonic creatures. At the center of the story is a vampire trying to find her long-lost sister. Her search leads her to a dubious informant, whose orders she is forced to carry out. The passage of Vampiress: Eternal Duet involves exploring dark locations and fighting opponents. The enemies here are not mindless extras. In battle, they are able to enter a state of Ethereal Madness, gaining access to devastating attacks. The signal for such a technique is the gleam in the enemy’s eyes, and a well-timed counterstrike allows him to be stunned, opening up the possibility of a brutal execution.
Game Screenshots &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;

Game Description Torrent Empire is a simulator of creating your own pirate empire, set in the scenery of the digital underground of the 2000s era. All activities related to the construction of a shadow content distribution network are presented in the format of a strategic project with an interface that simulates the command line of a terminal. The foundation for expanding influence is the successful administration of server infrastructure and methodical hacking of software. Gamers will have to immerse themselves in a complex justice system, where every action has its consequences and requires a balanced approach to decision making. The main task is to constantly increase capacity and attract new audiences for its underground network.
Activities in the illegal sector of the Internet inevitably involve constant threats and the need to carefully calculate every step. Law enforcement agencies are constantly hunting for violators, which forces them to look for sophisticated ways to avoid prosecution and act with the utmost caution. Every dubious deal in Torrent Empire forces you to look for a balance between potential benefits and risks. Only the most prudent and cunning will be able to achieve the status of a true digital legend, while any mistake can lead to the complete collapse of the entire enterprise and the loss of the progress achieved.
Game Screenshots &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;

Game Description Eternity Egg is a chaotic action-adventure platformer with a concept that harkens back to the 3D gaming era of the mid-90s. The visual component of the project deliberately uses stylized polygonal graphics with characteristic shiny surfaces, creating a distinctive and recognizable retro image. This bizarre world is inhabited by grotesque and sometimes awkward creatures, whose appearance perfectly complements the overall atmosphere of a surreal and unpredictable journey. An integral part of this experience is the high-energy electronic trance soundtrack, which sets a fast-paced and intense rhythm to everything that happens. The project is an exclusively single-player adventure, where the main emphasis is on dynamic exploration of the environment and overcoming platform challenges.
The central element of the gameplay formula is the unique physics of springy movements, allowing the protagonist to make incredibly high and long jumps. Mastering these mechanics becomes the key to successfully completing intricate levels designed with verticality in mind. The ability to control piloted mechs, which radically change the dynamics, brings significant variety to the process of exploring the world of Eternity Egg. By taking control of one of these giants, the hero gains access to powerful weapons and the ability to overcome previously insurmountable obstacles. Events are observed from a third-person perspective, which provides a comfortable overview and allows players to fully appreciate the scale of the locations.
Game Screenshots &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;

Game Description The Cradle is a horror film with a psychological bent, the narrative of which revolves around a reporter&rsquo;s investigation into the tragedy that unfolded within the walls of the Synergy Soft corporation. The main character named Alex needs to make a foray into an abandoned office complex to establish the true motives for the brutal massacre that occurred six months earlier. According to the official interpretation, the incident was caused by a collective clouding of reason, but the reality turns out to be much more frightening. Inside the structure, where the passage of time seems to have stopped, an unnatural silence reigns, and the shadows on the walls have acquired their own existence. Personal items and suicide messages left behind only add to the oppressive atmosphere of the empty work areas and the luxurious director&rsquo;s office.
Navigating through ominous corridors is directly related to the task of reconstructing the chronology of what happened. Achieving this goal requires collecting documentation and audio files that clarify the mystery of the failed experiment and the so-called Protocol of Silence. The ability to survive in The Cradle is determined by the ability to contain personal horror and not make unnecessary sounds, since sometimes the best strategy is absolute inaction. To uncover the secret, the character will have to search for keys to gain access to locked locations, as well as solve mental problems to discover hidden passages. The process involves a detailed exploration of the underground laboratory and hidden rooms, with a critical element being the collection of flashlight batteries to avoid being swallowed up in absolute darkness.
Game Screenshots &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;

Game Description Farmer’s Market Simulator is a project in which the central place is given to managing your own cozy market in the countryside. The customer service process includes scanning products, packaging them and providing a high level of service to build a loyal customer base. Financial transactions at the cash register require precision when accepting payments and issuing change. Successful trade directly depends on the competent organization of display cases and attractive display of collected products. The source of goods is not only the vegetable garden, but also livestock farming, which involves caring for chickens, cows and sheep to obtain fresh eggs, milk and wool. Caring for animals and keeping their pens clean become an integral part of a comfortable farm routine.
The basis of the entire enterprise is agriculture, starting with plowing the land, planting seeds and regular watering. The entire agricultural cycle in Farmer&rsquo;s Market Simulator is built on the gradual ripening of the crop, which requires attention and patience. To maintain the efficiency of the farm, it is possible to improve the inventory. Watching crops grow from seeds to full-fledged fruits gives a feeling of satisfaction from the work done. The gradual expansion of farmland and the improvement of working tools make it possible to build a prosperous country life step by step, turning a small farm into a thriving business.
Game Screenshots &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;

Game Description Breadbox is a detailed simulator that allows you to touch the golden era of computing in the 70s and 80s. The project offers accurate emulations of such iconic machines as the Commodore 64, VIC-20 and PET 2001-8. The core of the entire process is physical interaction with old-school hardware and storage media within a sophisticated environment. Gamers will have to work with floppy disks, cassettes and cartridges, listening to the authentic sound of their operation. Complete immersion in the atmosphere is facilitated by a visual style that reliably imitates the image on CRT monitors. Those who want to delve deeper into the topic have the opportunity to learn the basics of programming in BASIC languages ​​or 8-bit machine code.
The high level of simulation reliability is supported by modern technical solutions, including support for ultra-wide resolutions and emulator acceleration mode. For those new to Breadbox, there are tutorials that explain how to work with different media formats and how to download the software. The built-in media library simplifies access to vintage software, and flexible keyboard customization options increase ease of control. In addition to the simulator, the package includes a set of multi-player themed mini-games that focus on comedic interaction and testing trust. The organization of joint sessions is implemented through the room code system on Steam, as well as through integration with the Twitch platform chat.
Game Screenshots &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;

Game Description Bober Bros No Means Nothing is about violation of personal space and silent horror born from awkward pauses and hostile glances. The narrative places the hero in an oppressive atmosphere, where a mundane work shift at the packaging turns into a test of strength due to a colleague who constantly tests other people&rsquo;s boundaries. Attempts to relax at home also turn into failure due to noise from the neighboring apartment and mysterious holes in the walls. The source of fear here is not the supernatural, but a feeling of being cornered and growing psychological pressure. The visual execution of the project deliberately refers to the aesthetics of PS2-era horror, which only enhances the overall feeling of discomfort.
The central element of the mechanics is a system of interaction in which every word or lack thereof has irreversible consequences. Any response, be it agreement, a decisive refusal, or prolonged silence, changes the balance of power in relations with the source of the threat. The process of playing Bober Bros No Means Nothing encourages you to explore different models of behavior in a stressful situation. One of several possible endings directly depends on the chosen line of defense, the spectrum of which extends from a tense farewell to a truly chilling finale. The session duration, which does not exceed one hour, allows you to easily experiment with the consequences of your decisions.
Game Screenshots &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;

Game Description MineMogul is an opportunity to design and build a giant industrial complex in the bowels of the earth, where the main task is to tame chaos. The process is constantly complicated by unpredictable failures caused by a realistic physical model, which forces us to constantly search for creative solutions to keep the mechanisms working. The action takes place in a mysterious, deserted cave system, among the ruins of abandoned mining operations. Exploring these abandoned locations unlocks hidden resources and new secrets, and every cavern discovered holds potential for an ambitious tycoon. As production expands, the complexity only increases, making management a real challenge.
The basis of the gameplay is the creation of large-scale and interconnected production networks. You must navigate conveyor belts through winding shafts, connect different pieces of equipment, and use the laws of physics to create fully autonomous operations. At MineMogul, optimizing machine placement and finding innovative engineering approaches are the key to success. Overcrowded conveyors and parts flying around require constant monitoring and timely adjustment of the built system. The ultimate goal is to establish the smooth operation of the entire enterprise and achieve the status of an unrivaled industrial tycoon by subjugating the spontaneous disorder.
Game Screenshots &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;

Game Description Dummy Dungeon is a hardcore roguelight action game with a first-person view, where sharp reflexes and high concentration become the key to survival in a colorful but dangerous world. The gameplay is based on the choice of one of 24 unique heroes, whose specialization radically changes the approach to battles. For example, the Monk relies on a grappling hook for high maneuverability, while the Witch uses a cauldron to create powerful buffs in combat. The high dynamics of confrontations force you to constantly adapt to the situation, and the abundance of available characters allows you to form your own style of play, experimenting with different tactics and combinations of abilities.
The main goal of wandering through procedurally generated labyrinths is to rescue beautiful princesses. The journey through Dummy Dungeon takes you through many different locations, from dark catacombs to giant flying mechanisms filled with unique enemies. The progression system is built on modifying characteristics and weapons with the help of perks and unique improvements. The Arsenal is capable of completely changing the mechanics of its use - from simply setting it on fire to creating special zones or automatically chasing enemies. Each stage ends with a clash with a powerful boss, which makes the final fights especially intense.
Game Screenshots &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;

Game Description Fantasy Idle Dungeon is a role-playing adventure, the main concept of which is built around automated progression and collecting fantasy creatures. The path to power lies through exploration of many dangerous areas, including a mysterious tower, long-sealed ruins of ancient civilizations and snowy fields bound by eternal ice. Resources obtained in battles become the basis for the manufacture of exclusive equipment that can be adapted to specific needs. The system for improving it through enchanting, reforging and inlaying with precious stones allows you to turn epic items into legendary artifacts. Such modifications provide access to special attributes and additional effects, significantly strengthening the squad. Battles with bosses do not require constant control, since to activate them you just need to start the automatic mode and watch the triumph of your charges.
The central element of the mechanic is the acquisition and development of dozens of unique creatures called Jenin. Their improvement occurs through fusion, training using special skill books and subsequent transformation into their ultimate, most powerful forms. Strategic depth in Fantasy Idle Dungeon is achieved through flexible formation customization that takes into account the unique talents and attributes of each fighter on the team. This opens up the possibility of creating a variety of tactical styles, from aggressive high-damage offensive builds to impenetrable defensive configurations focused on counterattacks. Units continue to fight heroically and bring victories even in the absence of direct control, ensuring continuous advancement throughout the world.
Game Screenshots &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;

Game Description Ecopunk is a survival simulator in which the main goal is to restore the destroyed ecosystem of the planet through the unique mechanics of the Mother Tree. Planting ancient seeds can bring life back to devastated lands, and sacrificing defeated foes can bestow valuable blessings. The gradual healing of the climate and the rebirth of nature unlock the full power of this ancient creature, making the settlers stronger. In parallel with landscaping the territories, you will have to arrange your own settlement on the ruins of a former civilization. The construction process offers complete freedom, allowing you to build walls, houses and defensive structures cell by cell. For the community to prosper, it is necessary to master up to 8 different professions, including medicine, weaponry and cooking.
However, a hostile world does not forgive mistakes. The constant threat comes not only from hunger or disease, but also from extreme temperatures. To successfully withstand harsh conditions, Ecopunk requires the need to obtain food through hunting and farming. Creating reliable shelters with heating and cooling systems becomes the key to survival. In addition to climate challenges, mutants and rebellious machines pose a serious danger, with whom you will have to engage in mortal battles. Raiding enemy camps provides an influx of valuable resources, but requires protecting your own borders. The arsenal for protecting the colonists includes a variety of weapons, from pistols to heavy shotguns, and durable armor.
Game Screenshots &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;

Game Description The Art of Reflection is a first-person puzzle game where conventional physics gives way to surreal acrobatics. The protagonist will have to perform dizzying maneuvers that defy gravity and navigate intricate architectural labyrinths. A key tool for navigation is the ability to instantaneously approach, allowing you to cover significant distances in the blink of an eye. This mechanic also makes it possible to adjust the flight path in slow motion, opening up access to previously unreachable areas. The gameplay involves exploring locations with an inverted perspective, where the ceiling becomes the floor, and the usual logic of space stops working. The goal of each stage is to reach the final point.
The basis of everything is the concept of using mirrors not as reflective surfaces, but as full-fledged portals into inverted dimensions. In The Art of Reflection, in order to go through the looking glass, you must fulfill a certain condition. A red sphere should appear in the reflection, serving as a teleportation point and the only way to penetrate the distorted version of reality. This approach allows you to bypass obstacles, manipulate symmetry to solve problems, and even radically change the geometry of rooms. As you progress, the puzzles become more multifaceted, requiring the gamer to think outside the box and be willing to experiment to find the right path.
Game Screenshots &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;

Game Description No, I&rsquo;m not a Voenkom is a psychological thriller whose plot revolves around a sudden invasion of personal space. A sharp knock on the door becomes a catalyst for a whole series of tense events that test the protagonist&rsquo;s endurance. Every interaction with the outside world becomes a difficult choice between trying to remain safe and risking succumbing to destructive curiosity. The oppressive atmosphere of an old apartment, where the air is saturated with the smell of dust and paint, increases the feeling of isolation. The main gameplay is tied to a constant feeling of anxiety, and chases through dark, abandoned places become a real test of composure, making the heart pound at a frantic rhythm.
The main character is an ordinary factory worker leading a joyless existence in an unremarkable small town. His life was a predictable routine, consisting of a stable job and mortgage payments at an extortionate 89% per annum for his own home. However, this gray stability collapses one gloomy evening. In No, I&rsquo;m not a Voenkom, a familiar but worn-out and cluttered home becomes both the last bastion of safety and a death trap. Despite all the surrounding chaos, it is this cramped, uncomfortable space that feels like the only place that can be considered home.
Game Screenshots &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;

Game Description Ragnar is a roguelike game set in Norse mythology, where the main goal is to confront the god of deception Loki and his attempt to change the fate of Ragnarok. A system of dynamic progression and permanent improvements allows you to become more powerful with each new foray into changing worlds. You can combine divine blessings, abilities, and legendary weapons to create your own fighting style. For example, you can combine the power of Tyr&rsquo;s Spear of Justice with Freya&rsquo;s Phantom Ambush, forming unique tactical combinations to crush your enemies. Traveling through the worlds involves choosing your own path, which directly determines the complexity of the upcoming tests and the value of the rewards received. Each trip opens up new routes and mysterious dungeons, branching out from the world tree Yggdrasil.
Wanderings take place across nine worlds, from majestic palaces to gloomy and dangerous depths. Each kingdom is filled with a unique atmosphere and dangers, be it icy labyrinths or enchanted forests. During the adventure you will have to enlist the help of such familiar characters as Thor, Freya, Heimdall and Eitri. Interaction with allies in Ragnar directly affects the development of the saga, placing the hero at the very center of unfolding events. It is their help that will become a support in the fight against legendary opponents and giants released into freedom. The main goal is to confront the chaos that Loki unleashed on the worlds and overthrow him from his throne in order to become a light in the darkest days of Norse mythology.
Game Screenshots &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;

Game Description Lonely House is an opportunity to transform a secluded building at a city crossroads into a unique art object. The project proposes to focus solely on the external design, giving complete control over a small isolated plot of land. Enthusiasts have at their disposal a wide range of tools for customizing the building, allowing them to change the style of the walls and adjust its height. Decoration of the facade is carried out using a variety of objects: from overgrown bushes and ventilation systems to stylish neon signs with customizable lighting. You can even add graffiti to the walls or add accessories to the sidewalk, giving the building a unique character.
The entire creative process is accompanied by soothing lo-fi melodies, creating a meditative and completely leisurely atmosphere, free of any pressure. Lonely House&rsquo;s gameplay is based on the idea of ​​finding aesthetics in imperfection, proving that even the most neglected buildings have their own charm. Boarded-up windows are no longer ugly when they are covered with creeping ivy, and bright lights bring a touch of life to a dark intersection. For complete immersion in creating the desired mood, you have the opportunity to control the position of the sun and weather conditions. Thus, everyone can create their own unique corner of tranquility in the middle of a noisy metropolis.
Game Screenshots &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;

Game Description Motorhome: Traveling North America 2 is a collectible version of the project, whose main task is a measured movement through the most colorful locations of the United States. Gameplay revolves around overcoming mental puzzles and discovering cleverly hidden objects while visiting a variety of locations, from grandiose national parks to comfortable coastal areas. This special edition expands the scope of the ride with 10 additional stages featuring a comical animal to help you discover items. The version also includes over-the-top puzzles and unique memorabilia to add to your collection.
The foundation of the gameplay is an expedition in a personal motorhome, providing a feeling of unlimited mobility. The route runs through canyons, ski resorts and other points characteristic of the North American continent. Successfully adding to Motorhome&rsquo;s memorabilia collection requires constant concentration. Advancement is achieved through a series of activities: discovering hundreds of hidden things in realistic images, completing calming mini-funs like finding discrepancies or making jigsaw puzzles, and completing challenges to practice memory.
