Game Description Unseen is a psychological horror game whose main objective is to immerse yourself in an oppressive and mysterious atmosphere. The project is implemented in the format of a walking simulator, where the narration is from the first person. The gameplay is deliberately devoid of overloaded elements, concentrating on exploring locations and interacting with interactive objects. The process of exploring the environment and solving a few puzzles serve as the main tools for building suspense. Sound plays an important role in creating a feeling of isolation. The photorealistic visual component further enhances the effect of presence, making you feel increasing psychological pressure.
At the center of the story is John, a specialist in forensic photography. After completing an unexpectedly long and grueling shift, circumstances force him to seek temporary shelter for the night. What is initially perceived as an opportunity for a short rest quickly transforms into a series of alarming events. The gameplay of Unseen forces the protagonist to encounter frightening and inexplicable phenomena in a confined space. A seemingly harmless place begins to demonstrate its sinister essence, turning an ordinary night into a real test for the psyche. Every discovery and every new detail only deepens his paranoia.
Game Screenshots &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;

Game Description Morphos is a psychological horror in which the line between reality and madness is blurred within the walls of a mysterious scientific complex. Exploring the dark underground corridors involves solving numerous puzzles and confronting anomalous phenomena. The space around is constantly changing, turning into intricate labyrinths and distorting the usual perception. Survival will require stealthy movement, competent management of resources and the use of various types of weapons for self-defense from monsters. Meetings with opponents and sudden frightening events keep you in constant suspense, and traps placed everywhere force you to act with extreme caution. Gameplay is also complicated by temporary anomalies affecting the environment. You can save progress only in special safe rooms that serve as an island of calm.
The storyline revolves around a man who recently left the walls of a psychiatric hospital after losing his memory. His wife, a research scientist, gets him a job on her team, wanting to help him return to a normal life and look after him. The new place of work for the protagonist in Morphos becomes the same ominous underground facility where dubious experiments are carried out. At first, what is happening seems routine, but soon inexplicable things begin to happen. The player will not only have to find artifacts and keys for advancement, but also participate in dialogues with the ability to choose lines that influence the development of events. The story culminates in a fight with an extremely dangerous final boss.
Game Screenshots &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;

Game Description Organized Inside is a meditative puzzle game in which the process of cleaning becomes a metaphor for personal growth and transformation. The project invites you to immerse yourself in the leisurely systematization of everyday objects, being completely devoid of timers, points or health bars. The main emphasis is on relaxation and finding harmony in the chaos of everyday life. The narrative unfolds through the stories of five strangers whose secrets must be unraveled by putting their things in order. On this journey, players are accompanied by a cat mentor, providing useful advice and creating a cozy atmosphere. The gameplay allows you not only to find the perfect place for each thing, but also to gradually discover the joy and meaning of life.
Players will encounter cluttered spaces such as kitchen countertops, cabinets, or car interiors. The challenge is to place all the items neatly, which sometimes feels like solving a spatial puzzle. Some objects can be stacked or stacked, while others require pre-washing before taking their place. The Organized Inside project offers over a thousand familiar items for organization. Control is implemented entirely using the mouse, and the isometric perspective provides a convenient overview for putting things in perfect order. Finding hidden items within others adds an extra layer of exploration to the gameplay.
