Game Description The Holiday Story is a psychological horror film with a first-person perspective. The events of the game take place on the eve of 1982, completely immersing you in a festive environment. The project meticulously recreates the retro style of the 80s, visually processed to match the characteristic aesthetics of VHS tapes. The initially welcoming and bright atmosphere of the elegantly decorated store is gradually replaced by an oppressive feeling of inexplicable anxiety. This feeling is reinforced by realistic audio, encouraging you to react sensitively to every sound. Behind the sparkling garlands and bright shop windows, something threatening lurks, capable of turning the New Year&rsquo;s bustle into a real nightmare at any moment.
The plot focuses on the story of an ordinary person returning from a business trip. His only goal is to be on time to buy a gift for his son, to whom he promised a construction set for Christmas. His search leads him to a lit-up store full of toys, electronics, and videotapes. This place, however, turns out to be not at all what it seems at first. The process of exploring a store in The Holiday Story leads to encounters with anomalous events, during which familiar objects begin to behave unpredictably. The hero will have to find out what secret is hidden within the walls of the establishment, where a festive fairy tale turns into a frightening reality before our eyes.
Game Screenshots &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;    &times;

Game Description SCHROTT is a roguelike racing game where performing crazy stunts and collecting valuable loot provide the basis for deep vehicle customization. Instead of ordinary machines, there are absurd designs that lend themselves to all sorts of improvements to wreak even more chaos. Each race turns into a hunt for resources that allow you to turn your car into a unique weapon of destruction on the road. Arcade controls make the gameplay accessible and intuitive from the first minutes, and high-speed action does not let you relax. The rides take place along procedurally generated tracks designed in the style of JunkPunk, which ensures that each new playthrough is unique and forces you to constantly adapt to changing conditions.
The central character of this dynamic project is a raccoon who gets behind the wheel to create total chaos. The variety in SCHROTT comes not only from the numerous upgrades, but also from the other available drivers. Among them you can choose a penguin or a rabbit, each of which has its own passive skills that affect your driving style. Travel is not limited to one type of terrain, offering 3 maps and a completely new biome to explore. Two additional abilities expand your arsenal of techniques for performing spectacular maneuvers. A random loot system and special bonuses for equipment sets make each session unpredictable.
