Game Description The Sushi House is a first-person story-driven adventure where something unsettling and inexplicable lurks behind the façade of an ordinary sushi restaurant. A gradually growing sense of unease becomes the main driver of the narrative, involving us in unraveling the secrets of this place. The initially calm atmosphere gives way to a depressing foreboding, when routine duties begin to seem like part of an ominous mechanism. Every creaking floorboard and unusual shadow makes you doubt the reality of what is happening. Interactive dialogue helps immerse you deeper into the unfolding story, and the entire experience is a short but memorable 1-2 hour solo adventure.
The narrative starts from the first working day of the protagonist, who gets a part-time job. Under the guidance of a more experienced colleague, he will have to master the basics of managing an establishment, from cleaning the premises to serving visitors. One of the central mechanics of The Sushi House is a realistic cooking system that requires attention to detail when creating rolls. It is while performing these seemingly innocuous tasks that the player begins to notice subtle but disturbing inconsistencies that disrupt the daily routine. Immersive first-person gameplay enhances the immersive experience, allowing you to fully experience the ominous transformation of the atmosphere.
