Game Description Mercantile Might is a detailed ruler simulator that asks you to take control of a small medieval settlement and lead it to prosperity through competent strategic planning. The basis for future greatness is social institutions, because it is a strong system of health care, education and law and order that distinguishes a great city from a simple settlement. The creation of a developed healthcare and education system allows not only to improve the quality of life of citizens and ensure the stability of the population, but also to accelerate technological progress. To do this, it is necessary to build a complex infrastructure, including roads, residential areas and other functional facilities that make the city attractive to new residents.
However, the stability of society is impossible without a strong economic base. It is necessary to establish trade relations with other cities to ensure the flow of resources and expand markets for their own goods. To achieve these goals, Mercantile Might provides a wide range of tools. The ruler&rsquo;s arsenal includes over 65 unique buildings for urban development and more than 300 technologies for research, opening up new opportunities. As the city grows and the population increases, their needs will steadily increase, presenting the gamer with new management and strategic tasks to optimize the costs and lives of citizens.
