Game Description Auridia is a pixel action platformer in which gamers must descend into the depths of an abandoned underground kingdom to uncover its secrets. The journey takes you through an interconnected world of caves and mysterious biomes, where every corner holds a piece of past history. The structure of the world, made in the best traditions of metroidvanias, encourages returning to already explored locations with a new arsenal of skills. Advancement in depth directly depends on the tools found and the abilities mastered, which open up previously inaccessible paths. The narration is not told directly, but through the study of dozens of artifacts and communication with non-player characters, which allows you to independently piece together the picture of the events that took place.
Completing platform challenges requires mastering a variety of techniques, including parrying attacks, throwing objects, and using a climbing hook. To solve puzzles and access secret areas, you need to combine several skills at the same time. Unique skills such as Kinesis for object manipulation and Distortion Sphere for instant movement deserve special mention. The passage of Auridia is closely connected with the study of lore, because only by studying relics and coming into contact with forgotten gods can one learn the fate of characters like Snorri and Icarion. Hidden passages maintain the constant feeling that a new discovery awaits around every corner.
